#
# Counter-example for math:PersistenceModuleLifetimeConflationShape: ONE node
# typed BOTH math:PersistenceModule AND math:PersistenceLifetime — the whole algebraic functor
# P: (index poset) → Vect conflated with the birth–death interval of a SINGLE feature. They are
# held owl:disjointWith by a DIRECT axiom (both descend from math:MathematicalObject, so the
# disjointness is NOT entailed by their parents), so the sh:not [ sh:class math:PersistenceLifetime ]
# derived on math:PersistenceModule fires — shacl.NotConstraintComponent
# (math:PersistenceModuleLifetimeConflation).
# ISOLATION: the node is COMPLETE for BOTH kinds — its math:moduleIndex and math:structureMap
# satisfy the persistence-module frame, and its math:overFiltration, math:persistenceFeature,
# math:bornAt and math:diesAt satisfy the persistence-lifetime frame (an essential H0 component,
# diesAt math:PositiveInfinity) — so ONLY the sh:not fires, EXACTLY ONE finding. Every supporting
# object (the filtration, the homology group) is well-formed for its own shape.
# Back-reference: math:PersistenceModuleLifetimeConflation (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Wired exactly like counter-examples/calibration-sense-conflation.ttl.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecPersistenceModuleLifetimeConflation).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

# ONE node typed BOTH kinds, complete for each, so only the conflation fires.
ex:conflated a math:PersistenceModule , math:PersistenceLifetime ;
    math:moduleIndex ex:indexPoset ;             # completes the module frame
    math:structureMap ex:transition ;            # completes the module frame
    math:overFiltration ex:filtration ;          # completes the lifetime frame
    math:persistenceFeature ex:h0Component ;     # completes the lifetime frame
    math:bornAt ex:eps ;                         # completes the lifetime frame
    math:diesAt math:PositiveInfinity .          # essential feature: never dies within the filtration

ex:indexPoset a math:MathematicalObject .
ex:transition a math:MathematicalObject .

# The filtration the lifetime is read over: a well-formed single-parameter math:Filtration.
ex:filtration a math:Filtration ;
    math:filtrationAmbient ex:ambient ;
    math:filtrationIndexKind math:lengthDimension ;
    math:hasFiltrationStage ex:stage .
ex:ambient a math:TopologicalSpace .
ex:stage a math:FiltrationStage ;
    math:filtrationThreshold ex:eps ;
    math:stageStructure ex:cx .
ex:cx a math:TopologicalSpace .

# The feature the lifetime tracks: an essential H0 component (a well-formed abelian group).
ex:h0Component a math:HomologyGroup ;
    math:underlyingSet ex:h0Carrier ;
    math:structureOperation ex:h0Addition ;
    math:satisfiesAxiom ex:h0CommutativityAxiom .
ex:h0Carrier a math:Set .
ex:h0Addition a math:Operation .
ex:h0CommutativityAxiom a math:MathematicalObject .

ex:eps a math:Quantity ; math:quantityValue "0.10"^^xsd:decimal .
<http://example.org/math/eps> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
